  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1200 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nTowards the end of the week, the aforementioned shortwave \ntrough continues to pivot north/northeast of the forecast area, \nwith another system pushing into the western CONUS bringing \nsouthwesterly winds aloft. This will usher in even warmer \ntemperatures, continuing the gradual warm- up and above normal \nhighs. With the NBM temperature interquartile range only showing\na 3-4 degree difference between the 25th and 75th percentiles, \nthere's fairly high confidence in highs reaching the upper 60s \nto low 70s both Thursday and Friday.\n\nPrecipitation chances then increase this weekend as the upper\nlevel system continues to push east towards the area on\nSaturday. Latest guidance has slowed down the system a bit and slightly\nincreased rain chances to 10-20% Saturday afternoon and 40-60% \nSaturday evening into the overnight hours. Additionally, latest\nNBM probabilities showcase a 30-50% chance of at least 0.10\"\nrainfall (about a 10% increase from previous guidance) and a\n25-35% chance of at least 0.25\", mainly northwest of the\nInterstate-44 corridor. As the previous forecast mentioned,\nlimited instability will keep any thunderstorm chances below\n10%.\n\nBehind this system, cooler air will filter into the area, with\nafternoon temperatures remaining in the upper 40s and 50s\nheading into the beginning of next week.",
